# Marquise Cut Three Stone Engagement Ring ({{year}}): 3 Flanker Rules Save $3K

![Three loose marquise cut diamonds held in jeweller tweezers against a soft grey backdrop as the DiamondCritics featured image for the {{year}} marquise cut three stone engagement ring guide titled 3 flanker rules save three thousand dollars](/images/marquise-three-stone-engagement-ring.jpg "Marquise Cut Three Stone Engagement Ring 3 Flanker Rules Save Three Thousand Dollars")

## TL;DR — Marquise Three Stone Engagement Ring in One Scroll

**A marquise three stone engagement ring is a centre marquise with two accent diamonds on each side.** The accent stones are called flankers. Pick the right flankers and the ring reads balanced, meaningful, and worth every dollar. Pick the wrong flankers and the centre gets drowned, the budget overshoots by $3,000, and the ring looks dated inside a year.

**The 3 flanker rules that save $3K (all 3 covered in full below):**

- **Rule 1 — Match the flanker shape to the centre marquise.** Trillion, round, and pear are the only three shapes that work. Trapezoid works at 2ct+ centres. Round brilliants on a 1ct marquise look awkward in half the lightings.
- **Rule 2 — Keep flankers at 1:3 carat ratio to the centre.** A 1ct centre needs 0.33ct total flankers (0.17ct each). Flankers bigger than 1:2 drown the marquise. Flankers smaller than 1:4 disappear.
- **Rule 3 — Match flanker metal to centre basket metal.** White gold centre basket + yellow gold flankers reads as a cheap retrofit. Pick one metal family — platinum, white, yellow, or rose — and stay in it across all three stones.

→ Entry pick: **[Marquise Cut Lab Three Stone in 14k White Gold at $1,620](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/marquise-cut-lab-grown-diamond-three-stone-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-315104?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** — lab marquise flankers already matched to centre shape.
→ Natural centre pick: **[Marquise Cut Three Stone in 14k Yellow Gold at $1,970](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/marquise-cut-diamond-three-stone-engagement-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-by-james-allen-item-315107?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** — natural marquise flankers in yellow gold.
→ Trillion flanker pick: **[Three-Stone Trillion in 14k Rose Gold at $3,255](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/three-stone-trillion-diamond-engagement-ring-in-14k-rose-gold-1-3-ct-tw-item-203662?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** — trillion flankers deliver the classic three-stone silhouette.
→ Platinum pick: **[Lace Bridge Three Stone + Pavé in Platinum at $3,395](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/lace-bridge-three-stone-and-pave-diamond-engagement-ring-in-platinum-1-2-ct-t-w-item-197218?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** — platinum + vintage lace detail.

**Priority:** flanker choice decides whether this ring looks like $5,000 or $15,000 on the finger. Match the shape, keep the ratio, lock the metal. The 3 rules above cost nothing extra at order and prevent the $3,000+ mistake that pushes buyers from "I love this ring" to "I wish I had done this differently." See the full [marquise cut diamond guide](/marquise-cut-diamond) for shape fundamentals.

