## Three-Stone vs Solitaire vs Halo for Marquise

A three-stone is one of three main setting families for marquise. Quick comparison:

<table class="dc-custom-table"><thead><tr><th>Setting Family</th><th>Setting Cost</th><th>Tip Protection</th><th>Visual Carat</th><th>What this means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Solitaire</strong></td><td>$790–$2,850</td><td>Depends on prongs</td><td>1x stone</td><td>Classic look. See <a href="/marquise-solitaire-engagement-ring">solitaire guide</a>.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Halo</strong></td><td>$1,255–$5,985</td><td>High</td><td>~1.5x stone</td><td>Bigger-looking stone. See <a href="/marquise-halo-engagement-ring">halo guide</a>.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Three-Stone</strong></td><td>$1,620–$24,800</td><td>Partial (flankers protect shoulders)</td><td>1x centre + flanker carat</td><td>Dramatic, symbolic. Our pick for meaning-driven buyers.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Hidden Halo</strong></td><td>$1,255–$3,230</td><td>Moderate</td><td>1x stone</td><td>Solitaire silhouette + side sparkle. See <a href="/marquise-hidden-halo-engagement-ring">hidden halo guide</a>.</td></tr></tbody></table>

**Verdict:** Three-stone wins on symbolic meaning (past-present-future). Solitaire wins on cleanest classic look. Halo wins on bigger face-up stone. Hidden halo wins on modern understated. Pick based on which quality matters most.

