## How to Verify a Marquise Three Stone Before You Buy

Three checks every ring must pass before you commit.

**Check 1 — Confirm flanker shape matches the centre.** Trillion, pear, or round for most centres. Trapezoid, marquise, or emerald-cut only at 2ct+ centres. If the listing shows a shape outside this list for your centre carat, pass or spec the correct shape at order.

**Check 2 — Confirm flanker total carat is 1/4 to 1/3 of the centre.** Divide the listing's "total flanker weight" by 2 for each flanker. Multiply by 3 — the result should equal your centre carat. If flankers are above half-centre or below quarter-centre, the composition is off.

**Check 3 — Confirm all three baskets are the same metal.** The 360° video shows the baskets clearly. If the centre basket metal differs from the flanker baskets, walk. [IGI](https://www.igi.org/) and [GIA 4Cs](https://4cs.gia.edu/) both certify loose stones only — the setting metal is on the retailer's listing.

I run these three checks before I quote any client on a three-stone ring. The three-stone is beautiful when shape, ratio, and metal all align. It is a $3,000 wasted investment when any one of those three fails.

